# Agent git workflow

Never edit on `main`. At the start of a task, create a dedicated branch and worktree, then do all remaining work there.

```bash
git fetch origin
git worktree add -b agent/<short-task-slug> ../commander-decks-<short-task-slug> origin/main
```

Reuse that worktree for the rest of the session. Do not share a branch or worktree with another agent. If already inside a unique `agent/*` worktree for this task, keep using it.

## Commits

Commit without waiting for the user to ask. After each coherent step (for example: save decklist, resolve cards, primer + README link), create a commit with a 1–2 sentence message focused on why.

- Do not amend published commits
- Do not commit secrets or unrelated shared-cache noise

## Finish

When the task is done:

1. Inspect the full diff; drop unrelated cache or registry files
2. `git push -u origin HEAD`
3. Open a ready-for-review PR (`draft: false`) summarizing what changed

Create the PR with `gh pr create --base main --head <branch>` and confirm it is not a draft. If `gh` is missing or unauthenticated, say so and return `https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/compare/main...<branch>?expand=1` instead.

Return the PR URL.

## Deck modification PRs

When a PR changes an existing `decks/<deck>/decklist.txt`, the body must include a Cards in / Cards out table with every card linked to Scryfall. Generate it rather than writing it by hand:

```bash
python3 .agents/skills/deck-workspace/scripts/deck_change_table.py decks/<deck> --base origin/main
```

Place the table under a `## Cards in / Cards out` heading, one row per swap, and explain the reasoning in prose around it. A deck PR that only adds a new deck does not need the table.
